# Step 28, the skill folders' read rule (the owner's call on reading a
# skill, docs/steps/28/answered.md, point 7, as the maintainers narrowed
# it): each of the user's own skills found outside the workspace gives the
# session a rule of its own that allows reading its folder. Broken one at a
# time, with the tests that must fail. A list of its own, so that the
# change can be dropped whole with it.

[break] skill-folders-get-no-rule
rule: Each of the user's own skills found outside the workspace gives the session a rule that allows reading its folder, in force before the first turn's calls.
file: crates/cineris-core/src/ext/found/pipeline.rs
in: Held::find_skills
find: lock(&reads).follow(&policy, folders)
replace: drop((reads, policy, folders))
caught-by:
    cineris-core::it skill_reads::a_users_skill_folder_is_read_unasked_and_its_rule_follows_the_skills_found
    cineris-core::it skill_reads::a_users_skill_that_is_not_found_has_no_rule

[break] a-skill-gone-keeps-its-rule
rule: A skill no longer found loses its rule at the turn's start that finds the skills again.
file: crates/cineris-core/src/ext/found/reads.rs
in: SkillReads::follow
find: let take_back: Vec<ApprovalId> = gone.into_iter().filter_map(|(_, id)| id).collect();
replace: let take_back: Vec<ApprovalId> = gone.into_iter().filter_map(|_| None).collect();
caught-by:
    cineris-core::it skill_reads::a_users_skill_folder_is_read_unasked_and_its_rule_follows_the_skills_found

[break] a-skill-added-gets-no-rule
rule: A skill found at a later turn's start gains its rule then.
file: crates/cineris-core/src/ext/found/reads.rs
in: SkillReads::follow
find: let known = self.held.iter().any(|(held, _)| same(held, &folder))
replace: let known = !self.held.is_empty()
caught-by:
    cineris-core::it skill_reads::a_users_skill_folder_is_read_unasked_and_its_rule_follows_the_skills_found

[break] a-revoked-rule-comes-back
rule: A skill's rule the user revoked is not given again in the session, though its folder drops out of a finding and is found again.
file: crates/cineris-core/src/ext/found/reads.rs
in: SkillReads::follow
find: let taken = policy.not_held(&ours);
replace: let taken = policy.not_held(&[]);
caught-by:
    cineris-core::it skill_reads::a_users_skill_folder_is_read_unasked_and_its_rule_follows_the_skills_found

[break] the-skills-rule-allows-writes
rule: A skill's rule allows reading its folder, and nothing else: a write there is asked about as before.
file: crates/cineris-core/src/policy.rs
in: EngineInForce::follow_reads
find: lifts: new
replace: lifts: new.iter().flat_map(|rule| [rule.clone(), cineris_protocol::lease::Rule { effect: cineris_protocol::lease::Effect::Write, ..rule.clone() }]).collect()
caught-by:
    cineris-core::it skill_reads::a_users_skill_folder_is_read_unasked_and_its_rule_follows_the_skills_found

[break] the-skills-rule-reaches-beside-its-folder
rule: A skill's rule covers its folder and what is below it, not a folder beside it whose name begins as its does.
file: crates/cineris-core/src/policy.rs
in: reading_below
find: pattern.push_str("/**");
replace: pattern.push_str("*/**");
caught-by:
    cineris-core::it skill_reads::a_users_skill_folder_is_read_unasked_and_its_rule_follows_the_skills_found
    cineris-core policy::tests::a_skills_rule_compiles_and_matches_its_own_folder_alone

[break] the-skills-rule-reaches-its-root
rule: A skill's rule covers its folder, not the root of skills it is in.
file: crates/cineris-core/src/ext/found/reads.rs
in: readable
find: .map(|skill| skill.folder.clone())
replace: .map(|skill| skill.folder.parent().unwrap_or_else(|| skill.folder.clone()))
caught-by:
    cineris-core::it skill_reads::a_users_skill_folder_is_read_unasked_and_its_rule_follows_the_skills_found

[break] a-folders-name-is-read-as-a-pattern
rule: A skill's rule names its folder as it is named: a character a path glob reads as a pattern is taken as itself.
file: crates/cineris-core/src/policy.rs
in: reading_below
find: '*' | '?' | '[' | '{' | '}' => {
replace: '\u{0}' => {
caught-by:
    cineris-core::it skill_reads::a_users_skill_that_is_not_found_has_no_rule
    cineris-core policy::tests::a_skills_rule_compiles_and_matches_its_own_folder_alone

[break] a-session-allow-beats-a-deny
rule: A deny rule still wins over a skill's rule, as it wins over any allow.
file: crates/cineris-policy/src/rules.rs
in: RuleSet::strongest
find: strength(compiled.rule.rule.action)
replace: strength(compiled.rule.rule.action) + 3 * u8::from(compiled.rule.source == RuleSource::Session)
packages: cineris-core
caught-by:
    cineris-core::it skill_reads::a_users_skill_folder_is_read_unasked_and_its_rule_follows_the_skills_found

[break] a-skill-in-the-workspace-gets-a-rule
rule: A user's skill whose folder is within the workspace, judged by place, gives no rule, and one moved there during the session loses its own: the workspace's reads and its look for secrets stay as they were.
file: crates/cineris-core/src/ext/found/reads.rs
in: readable
find: !location_within(&folder, workspace)
replace: !workspace.as_os_str().is_empty()
caught-by:
    cineris-core::it skill_reads::the_skills_in_the_workspace_have_no_rule
    cineris-core ext::found::reads::tests::a_folder_may_be_read_unasked_only_apart_from_the_workspace_and_below_the_home

[break] a-folder-that-holds-the-workspace-gets-a-rule
rule: A user's skill whose folder holds the workspace (its author working in its own scripts/) gives no rule, which would cover the whole workspace (M1 of the third review).
file: crates/cineris-core/src/ext/found/reads.rs
in: readable
find: && !location_within(workspace, &folder)
replace: && !workspace.as_os_str().is_empty()
caught-by:
    cineris-core::it skill_reads::a_skill_folder_that_holds_the_workspace_has_no_rule
    cineris-core ext::found::reads::tests::a_folder_may_be_read_unasked_only_apart_from_the_workspace_and_below_the_home

[break] the-home-directory-gets-a-rule
rule: A skill's folder that is the home directory or holds it gives no rule, which would be one for all of it (L3 of the third review).
file: crates/cineris-core/src/ext/found/reads.rs
in: readable
find: && home.is_none_or(|home| !location_within(home, &folder))
replace: && home.is_none_or(|_| true)
caught-by:
    cineris-core::it skill_reads::a_skill_folder_that_is_the_home_directory_has_no_rule
    cineris-core ext::found::reads::tests::a_folder_may_be_read_unasked_only_apart_from_the_workspace_and_below_the_home

[break] a-projects-skill-gets-a-rule
rule: Only the folders `readable` gives have a rule: a project's skills give none, trusted or not, and a file of theirs that looks like a secret is asked about as any file of the workspace's is.
